#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
HEXPYRION v8 - static Nuitka source recovery (authorized research preview)
by dimareverse | devirt / onefile-unpack / native reconstruction

Static mode is the default: no runtime hooks, no injection.
Use only on software you own or are authorized to inspect.

Recovery contract — translate NUITKA'S native language into Python:
  - Constants blob (mod_consts) + module table
  - Native x64 of Nuitka helpers (LOOKUP_ATTRIBUTE, CALL_FUNCTION_*,
    MAKE_FUNCTION_*, branches, iterators, …) → Python statements
  - f_lineno source maps + structured CFG / register simulation
  - NOT CPython .bytecode / pycdc (that is a different artifact; compiled
    Nuitka modules are native code, not marshalled .pyc)

NEW in v8 — direct rematerialization of the ORIGINAL Python (no C
reconstruction), payload-neutralized runtime capture, and universal
containers:

  --devirt      Static devirtualization with ZERO execution: every marshal'd
                code object in the ".bytecode" chunk is emitted 1:1 as .pyc
                (the original compiled Python bytecode, byte for byte), the
                ".files" chunk is unpacked, and native modules get constants
                pools + code-object maps. PE / ELF / Mach-O, standalone and
                onefile.

  --onefile-unpack
                Statically unpack any Nuitka onefile binary (zstd included)
                without ever executing the bootstrap.

  --trigger     Runtime "triggeratore": run under gdb, stop BEFORE any module
                code executes, dump the DECODED constants blob from process
                memory, then kill the process. The payload NEVER runs; the
                captured blob feeds the same static devirt pipeline (defeats
                in-memory/commercial blob protection).

Typical whole-binary emit:
  py nuitka_decompiler.py --source app.dll \\
      --emit-all-source out_source --only "pkg.*,__main__,__parents_main__"

Typical devirtualization:
  py nuitka_decompiler.py --source app.exe --devirt --devirt-decompile
  py nuitka_decompiler.py --source app.exe --trigger          # runtime blob
"""

